  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "A change to make sure that a query of type \"$value(Companies.Select(c => c.Employees))\" produces a flattened array of\n\t\t\temployees across all companies rather than array of arrays with each array having list of employees in specific company.\n\t\t\tThis behavior is more natural and useful in most cases.\n\t\t\tIf we want to group data by keys (company data) this will be done with a Group function (path element), that will be introduced\n\t\t\tin future release.\n\t\t\tNOTE: This was already working as expected when Where clause was using as in this example:$value(Companies.Select(c => c.Employees.Where(x => x.Salary > 100000))\".",
  "repository": "",
  "title": "JsonQL",
